  "comment": "Data for scripts/check_no_hardcoded_cases.py (gate check no-hardcoded-cases). Real cases are evaluation data (live-checks, tests, EVIDENCE, docs), never product code paths. identifiers holds what no rule derives (names, curated values); every identifier the eval items and the real-case files under evals/ name is derived at scan time (the tree's and the base's), so a new eval item needs no entry here. Never add allowlist entries for new code; the allowlist only covers code that existed when the check landed and is burned down by the deletion/general-intelligence workstream. Each entry suppresses one rule for one match key (identifier id, or file/symbol name for module_name) in one file through its expires date (UTC). The gate reads the allowlist from origin/main: a candidate can only remove or narrow entries, never add or extend one. An expired entry fails a candidate that changes its file (or --strict-expiry). ratchet lists the findings that existed when rule eval_reference (product code reaching evals/ or tests/) and the derived eval identifiers landed, by path, rule, match and occurrence (its index among that file's findings of the same rule and match; no line, so moving code passes): it may only shrink (an entry the base lacks is refused, an entry no finding matches fails as stale: remove it with the fix); see the checker docstring.",
